error[DS0105]: `inner join` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:16
  |
1 | from 'a.csv' | inner join 'b.csv' on k;
  |                ^^^^^^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: the join kind goes after `join`: `join kind = inner`

error[DS0105]: `FULL OUTER JOIN` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:2:16
  |
2 | from 'a.csv' | FULL OUTER JOIN 'b.csv' on k;
  |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: the join kind goes after `join`: `join kind = fullouter`

error[DS0105]: `right join` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:3:16
  |
3 | from 'a.csv' | right join 'b.csv' on k;
  |                ^^^^^^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: the join kind goes after `join`: `join kind = rightouter`

error[DS0105]: `LEFT ANTI JOIN` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:4:16
  |
4 | from 'a.csv' | LEFT ANTI JOIN 'b.csv' on k;
  |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: the join kind goes after `join`: `join kind = leftanti`

error[DS0105]: `CROSS JOIN` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:5:16
  |
5 | from 'a.csv' | CROSS JOIN 'b.csv'
  |                ^^^^^^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: DataScript has no cross join; to pair every row with every row, add the same constant column to both sides with `extend` and join on it
  = note: the kinds are `inner`, `leftouter`, `rightouter`, `fullouter`, `leftsemi`, `leftanti`, `rightsemi` and `rightanti`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'a.csv' | join kind = inner 'b.csv' on k;
    from 'a.csv' | join kind = fullouter 'b.csv' on k;
    from 'a.csv' | join kind = rightouter 'b.csv' on k;
    from 'a.csv' | join kind = leftanti 'b.csv' on k;
    from 'a.csv' | CROSS JOIN 'b.csv'
which still has errors:

error[DS0105]: `CROSS JOIN` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> fixed:5:16
  |
5 | from 'a.csv' | CROSS JOIN 'b.csv'
  |                ^^^^^^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: DataScript has no cross join; to pair every row with every row, add the same constant column to both sides with `extend` and join on it
  = note: the kinds are `inner`, `leftouter`, `rightouter`, `fullouter`, `leftsemi`, `leftanti`, `rightsemi` and `rightanti`
